":"Mandates budgetary line items for the Center for Innovation for Care and Payment, transportation reimbursements, and expanded community care contracting.","evidence":"The Secretary shall include in the budget justification materials submitted to Congress... specific identification, as a budgetary line item, of the amounts required","evidence_verified":false,"key":"fiscal","score":50},{"assessment":"Amends multiple sections of title 38, United States Code, codifying access standards, adding new mental health screening mandates, establishing self-service online modules, and creating a pilot program.","evidence":"To improve the provision of care and services under the Veterans Community Care Program of the Department of Veterans Affairs, and for other purposes.","evidence_verified":true,"key":"scope","score":80},{"assessment":"Institutes permanent statutory updates to VA health care programs, alongside specific multi-year reporting requirements and a three-year pilot program.","evidence":"establish a three-year pilot program in not fewer than five locations to allow veterans... to access outpatient mental health and substance use services","evidence_verified":false,"key":"duration","score":70}],"missing_information":["Total net cost of implementing the various new screening, transportation, and pilot program requirements."],"rationale":"Sweeping legislation modifying Department of Veterans Affairs community care eligibility standards, mental health treatment programs, clinical appeals processes, and establishing new online tools and pilot programs.","score":75},"importance_meta":{"generated_at":"2026-10-26T07:44:06+00:00","model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","source_basis":"text+summary","source_urls":["https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr740/BILLS-119hr740ih.htm"]},"introduced_date":"2025-01-28","is_demo":false,"label":"H.R. 740","latest_action":{"date":"2025-07-23","text":"Ordered to be Reported (Amended) by Voice Vote."},"members":[{"chamber":"House","district":"12",